  :body "# Comprehensive Registry: Future Refinements, Test Debt & Edge-Case Validation

**Document Version**: `1.0.0`  
**Date**: 2026-09-07  
**Scope**: Full Monorepo Ecosystem (Layer 0 Language Kernel, Layer 1 Identity/Mesh, Layer 2 Config/Data, Layer 3 Plugins/Bridges, Intel Observability, and APM Execution Substrates).

---

## 1. Executive Overview

This registry establishes an exhaustive catalog of test debt, potential edge cases, property-based testing targets, adversarial vectors, and future refinements across all repository modules. It serves as the backlog and quality contract for subsequent iterations following Phase 265 and the planning of Phase 266.

---

## 2. Domain-Specific Refinement & Test Catalog

### 2.1. Domain 1: Data Placement Optimizer & ASN Codec (`asl-codec/src/placement.asl`)

| ID | Focus Area | Target Component | Description / Potential Edge Case | Recommended Test Harness & Methodology | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **TD-101** | Sparse / Missing Keys | `asl-codec/placement` | Records in a collection with disjoint or optional fields (e.g. Record 1 has `(:id :name)`, Record 2 has `(:id :email)`). Columnar transposition must not shift column offsets or introduce misaligned vectors. | Fuzzing with sparse AST dictionaries; verify `(:id [1 2] :name [\"a\" nil] :email [nil \"b\"])` preserves exact index alignment. | P0 |
| **TD-102** | Deeply Nested Records | `asl-codec/placement` | Transposition of arrays of structs containing nested records or sub-arrays (e.g. `(:id 1 :meta (:env \"prod\" :tags [\"a\" \"b\"]))`). | Property-based roundtrip testing: `(columnar-to-aos (aos-to-columnar data)) == data` across 500 generated nested records. | P1 |
| **TD-103** | BPE Subtoken Density Invariants | `asl-codec/placement` | Exact tokenizer token counts vary across model tokenizers (Gemma, Llama, Claude, GPT-4). Verify that the $\\ge 25\\%$ token reduction claim holds across all target vocabularies. | Multi-tokenizer benchmark suite running BPE token count assertions across 5 standard tokenizer models on identical sample datasets. | P1 |
| **TD-104** | Table Alignment & Escaping | `asl-codec/placement` | Table placement format `([:col1 :col2] [[row1] [row2]])` with string cells containing quotes, spaces, escaped characters, and delimiters. | Syntax validation check ensuring generated table forms parse cleanly through `asl check` and `asl-codec` without delimiter distortion. | P0 |
| **TD-105** | Compaction Decision Thresholds | `asl-codec/placement` | Verify boundary conditions for `recommend-placement`: exactly 1 record, 2 records, 3 records, 0 columns, 1 column, 100 columns. | Unit boundary sweep asserting `placement-aos` is strictly returned for $N < 3$ or columns $< 2$. | P2 |

---

## 2.2. Domain 2: Dynamic ASL Expressions & Config Extensibility (`harness/src/config.asl`, `plugin.asl`)

| ID | Focus Area | Target Component | Description / Potential Edge Case | Recommended Test Harness & Methodology | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **TD-201** | Execution Quotas & Timeout | `harness/src/config.asl` | Executable ASL expressions embedded in `.asl.config.asn` could contain infinite loops `((df loop [] (loop)))` or deep recursion during config parsing. | Step-count bounded evaluator or timeout guard (e.g., max 1,000 reduction steps) in `evaluate-hook-predicate`. | P0 |
| **TD-202** | Purity & Capability Sandboxing | `harness/src/config.asl` | Configuration hook predicates must be pure queries and must not invoke host side-effects (e.g. shell execution or disk mutation). | Type-checker / linter rule asserting that functions called from config predicates are restricted to prelude math, logic, and string queries. | P0 |
| **TD-203** | Monotonic Security Overrides | `harness/src/config.asl` | A child configuration tier (worktree/subrepo) must never be able to re-enable a security feature disabled by global config (e.g. global `firewall: true` overridden by child `firewall: false`). | Adversarial unit test attempting to downgrade security constraints, asserting child override is rejected or ignored. | P0 |
| **TD-204** | Empty String & No-op Preservation | `harness/src/config.asl` | Empty raw configuration strings (`\"\"`) in cascaded tiers must act as no-ops rather than clobbering existing configuration records (preserving `config-test.asl:80` baseline). | Regression assertion verifying `(resolve-cascaded-config global-cfg \"\" \"\" \"\") == global-cfg`. | P1 |
| **TD-205** | Dynamic Tool Permission Hooks | `harness/src/plugin.asl` | Hook predicates dynamically filtering tools based on prompt classification and file path patterns (e.g. prohibiting write tools on `.asl/mem/intent.asn`). | Mock execution test: invoke write tool against protected path; assert hook predicate halts execution before tool invocation. | P1 |

---

## 2.3. Domain 3: 4-Tier Architectural Layer Stratification (`intel/src/health.asl`, `docs/LAYER_STRATIFICATION_SPEC.md`)

| ID | Focus Area | Target Component | Description / Potential Edge Case | Recommended Test Harness & Methodology | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **TD-301** | Transitive Inward Leakage | `intel/src/health.asl` | A Layer 0 module does not directly import Layer 1, but imports a Layer 2 module which re-exports or passes through Layer 1 identity types (`TaskContract`). | Transitive reachability analysis across module import DAG in `detect-layer-leakage`, flagging indirect layer violations. | P1 |
| **TD-302** | File-Level vs Package-Level Scoping | `intel/src/health.asl` | Currently `module-to-layer` classifies entire packages by prefix. Individual files within a package might cross layers (e.g., a utility file inside `agent-bus` that is purely Layer 0). | Finer-grained annotation or path-based rule checking (e.g. `:layer 0` pragma in module header). | P2 |
| **TD-303** | Batch RPC Error Resilience | `asl-daemon-host.mjs` | Batch RPC queries containing invalid AST, nonexistent operations, or unparseable S-expressions must return structured error steps rather than crashing daemon socket. | Adversarial RPC fuzzing suite sending malformed JSON/S-expressions; verify daemon survives and responds with `:status \"error\"`. | P0 |
| **TD-304** | Monorepo Growth Regression | `intel/tests/boundary_test.asl` | As new packages are introduced, they must automatically be assigned to a layer and audited without manual test updates. | Dynamic test checking that every package in `manifest.asn` is recognized by `module-to-layer` and never defaults to unclassified without failing. | P1 |

---

## 2.4. Domain 4: Observability, Hotspots & Diagramming (`intel/src/diagram.asl`, `health.asl`)

| ID | Focus Area | Target Component | Description / Potential Edge Case | Recommended Test Harness & Methodology | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **TD-401** | Complex Multi-Component Cycles | `intel/src/health.asl` | 3-state DFS cycle detector handling complex graphs with multiple disconnected strongly-connected components (SCCs) and self-loops. | Synthetic graph test fixtures with Tarjan SCC verification, asserting 100% detection of all distinct cyclic paths. | P1 |
| **TD-402** | Large-Scale Diagram Rendering | `intel/src/diagram.asl` | Diagram generation on codebases with $> 1,000$ modules; Mermaid syntax limits and string buffer ceilings in pure ASL evaluator. | Stress test generating Mermaid diagrams for 1,000 synthetic nodes; verify zero buffer truncation and balanced Mermaid syntax. | P2 |
| **TD-403** | Blast-Radius Hotspot Calibration | `intel/src/health.asl` | Highly central utility modules (`asl-parser/lexer`, `asl-codec/asn`) have naturally high fan-in. Distinguish benign standard library primitives from architectural bottlenecks. | Weighted PageRank or betweenness centrality scoring to supplement raw fan-in counts. | P2 |

---

## 2.5. Domain 5: Normative RAG, BM25 & Intent Ledger (`asl-text`, `mem/bm25`, `.asl/mem/intent.asn`)

| ID | Focus Area | Target Component | Description / Potential Edge Case | Recommended Test Harness & Methodology | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **TD-501** | Incremental Index Invalidation | `mem/src/engine.asl` | When source files are edited, the resident in-memory vector and BM25 index must update incrementally via WAL without re-indexing all 530+ files. | Automated test modifying 1 file, asserting `:find` returns updated text immediately while maintaining index cache for unchanged files. | P1 |
| **TD-502** | Extreme Document Lengths in BM25 | `mem/src/bm25.asl` | BM25 length normalization penalty ($b=0.75$) behaving erratically on extreme document sizes (a 5-word heading vs a 50,000-word log dump). | Parameter sweep assertions proving normalized scores remain monotonically ranked and bounded within $[0, 1]$. | P2 |
| **TD-503** | Intent Drift Detection | `.asl/mem/intent.asn` | Automated pre-commit git hook asserting that every PR modifying architectural logic contains a corresponding Decision Record or Intent Shortcode (`d-xxxx`, `r-xxxx`). | Static audit script running in CI / Gate 3 verifying intent ledger alignment against modified files. | P1 |

---

## 2.6. Domain 6: APM, Process Streaming & Resource Guards (`asl-sh`, `agent-bus`, Phases 262–264)

| ID | Focus Area | Target Component | Description / Potential Edge Case | Recommended Test Harness & Methodology | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **TD-601** | High-Volume OOB Stream Demux | `asl/packages/asl-sh` | Commands generating megabytes of output per second (e.g. `yes`, continuous compiler builds, network traces) overwhelming memory buffers. | Stress test streaming 100MB stdout through APM OOB demuxer; assert evaluator heap remains $< 64\\text{MB}$ and process terminates cleanly. | P0 |
| **TD-602** | Spool Disk Cap Enforcement | `asl/packages/asl-sh` | Circular ephemeral disk spool (`/tmp/asl-proc-*.spool`) hard 10MB cap: file size must never exceed 10MB under any circumstances. | Write test generating 50MB into spool; assert file size on disk is truncated or ring-buffered to exactly $\\le 10\\text{MB}$. | P0 |
| **TD-603** | Stdin Deadlock & Process Teardown | `asl/packages/asl-sh` | Interactive commands prompting for user stdin (e.g. `sudo`, `read`) hanging unattended in agent batch runs. | Subprocess watchdog test: spawn hanging `cat`; assert watchdog sends `SIGTERM` at 10s and `SIGKILL` at 12s, returning structured exit receipt. | P0 |
| **TD-604** | Zombie Process Sweeper | `agent-bus/src/mesh.asl` | Process crashing or parent agent killed abruptly, leaving orphan child processes bound to network sockets or RAM. | Process group cleanup fixture asserting all PIDs in `ProcessNode` registry are cleanly terminated on task contract completion. | P1 |

---

## 2.7. Domain 7: Peripheral Grounding & FFI (`asl-quantum`, `asl-arduino`, `voice`)

| ID | Focus Area | Target Component | Description / Potential Edge Case | Recommended Test Harness & Methodology | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| **TD-701** | Virtual Peripheral Mock Drivers | `asl-arduino`, `voice` | Grounding peripheral packages beyond `:status \"conceptual-schema\"` using virtual loopback devices (e.g. virtual serial port / WASM audio sink). | Falsifiable test suite exercising real serial packet framing and PCM audio buffer serialization against loopback drivers. | P2 |
| **TD-702** | Quantum Circuit Simulation Truth | `asl-quantum` | Replacing conceptual gates with a lightweight deterministic state-vector simulator in pure ASL for 2-qubit to 4-qubit circuits (Bell states, GHZ). | Falsifiable test assertions verifying exact probability amplitudes: $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(\\|00\\rangle + \\|11\\rangle)$. | P2 |

